.TH SHOAL-KERNEL 1 "July 2026" "Shoal 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shoal-kernel \- run the resident Shoal execution kernel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shoal-kernel
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Serves authenticated Shoal sessions over a private Unix socket or one inherited connected Unix stream.
It owns durable session, task, event, PTY, journal, and execution state.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-session " NAME"
Select the default session.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
Listen on PATH after enforcing secure ownership and type checks.
.TP
.BI \-\-state-dir " PATH"
Store durable state below PATH.
.TP
.BI \-\-token-store " PATH"
Use PATH as the credential authority file; overrides
.BR SHOAL_TOKEN_STORE .
.TP
.BI \-\-policy " FILE"
Load the sandbox policy from FILE.
.TP
.BI \-\-embedded-fd " FD"
Serve one inherited connected AF_UNIX stream and do not open a public listener.
.TP
.B \-\-detach-stderr-after-ready
Close inherited standard error after announcing listener readiness. Explicit supervisors use this
to preserve startup diagnostics without retaining a captured pipe for the daemon lifetime.
.B \-\-require-token
Require bearer authentication on the public socket.
.TP
.B \-\-require-peer-uid
Require the public peer UID to match the kernel process.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-connections " N"
Bound simultaneous client connections.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-sessions " N"
Bound resident sessions.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-tasks-per-session " N"
Bound tasks owned by one session.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-ptys-per-session " N"
Bound PTYs owned by one session.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-ptys-per-principal " N"
Bound PTYs owned by one authenticated principal.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-ptys-global " N"
Bound all resident PTYs.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-subscriptions-per-session " N"
Bound event subscriptions owned by one session.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-blob-decompressions-per-window " N"
Bound decompression work admitted in one accounting window.
.TP
.BI \-\-blob-decompression-window-ms " N"
Set the decompression accounting window in milliseconds.
.TP
.BI \-\-frame-read-timeout-ms " N"
Bound time spent receiving one request frame.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Print complete transport and limit help.
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Print the version.
.SH OUTPUT
Listener mode announces readiness and its socket on standard error.
Embedded mode writes one bounded JSON readiness frame to the inherited descriptor.
.SH ERRORS
The kernel refuses invalid limits, unsafe socket paths, invalid or unrelated descriptors,
conflicting transports, unusable state or token stores, and invalid policies.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
shoal-kernel --session default --require-peer-uid
shoal-kernel --socket /run/user/1000/shoal/ci.sock --require-token
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 after an orderly shutdown and 1 for configuration, state, transport, or serving failures.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shoal (1),
.BR shoal-token (1),
.BR shoal-mcp (1)
